        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p class=\"has-drop-cap wp-block-paragraph\">MILWAUKEE &#x2014; Kat Zilka sat on the floor of her living room, beside a glowing Christmas tree and a pile of essays, and felt like weeping. It was late in 2022, and she had asked her 12th grade digital journalism students to reflect on their relationships to devices.&#xa0;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&#x201c;The things they were writing were deeply disturbing,&#x201d; she said.&#xa0;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/13/phone-addiction-young-people-fight-back-attention-activism/?utm_campaign=rss\">Read the rest&hellip;</a></p>"
